#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128946 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/id #uuid "b4697448-d5f7-59ae-86a1-689ae00ebb73" :question/math-academy-id "e-7197" :question/problem "The region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and $x=y^3-4y$, and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/ad479776abe1b64937bf9c79c413a827.png)" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/f0e34c7f4bb3ec1fc5266af37fe73361.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: -2 \\leq y \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∬_(D)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D_{1})dA + ∬_(D_{2})dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}∫_{0}^{y^{3} - 4y}dxdy + ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{2y^{3} - 2y}^{0}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{y^{3} - 4y}dy + ∫_{0}^{1}[x]_{2y^{3} - 2y}^{0}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}(y^{3} - 4y)dy + ∫_{0}^{1}(2y - 2y^{3})dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{4}}{4} - 2y^{2}]_{-2}^{0} + [y^{2} - \\frac{y^{4}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 4 + \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128947 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "9a106b26-c6fe-5e4b-ae43-9cc02ddb67c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7198" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x$, $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and lines $x=0$ and $y=2$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/44c00a18090dd9acfb716d4de0839aed.png)" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/dfed9d77548799c30e813d5415b96807.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∬_(D_{1})f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D_{2})f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2^{x}}f(x, y)dydx + ∫_{1}^{4}∫_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x, y)dydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "be10aba9-930e-54c3-814d-8d089757affc" :question/math-academy-id "e-7199" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x$, and the lines $y=1$, $x=1$, and $x=e$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/90badcdff8d1723816783ecee432d5a9.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n$$\ny = 2 + \\ln x \\mid ⟹x = e^{y - 2}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/97aa046fce141be1472a9103f7079cae.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 2 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∬_(D_{1})f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D_{2})f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{1}^{e}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{2}^{3}∫_{e^{y - 2}}^{e}f(x, y)dxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99a9e816-28e8-56f3-beb0-f84570f18f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/3}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127113} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a7d48-37b0-5d6e-9093-0756a97cef84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{6 - y}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/2}^{y/3}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127114} {:answer/id #uuid "df24c72c-7874-571d-95cd-c83af5cc06c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127115} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e2debd-3524-5015-9348-c1930de0e879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127116} {:answer/id #uuid "78030bc8-8d41-503d-b6c4-f8acdc3741f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y - 6}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y/3}^{y - 6}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5e2debd-3524-5015-9348-c1930de0e879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{9}∫_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{9}^{12}∫_{y - 6}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127116} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e11bd0-c56d-528e-9571-41f1adad3049" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127112}] :question/id #uuid "75185755-8578-56f9-bff0-716550a71de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-37757" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/q-37757.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y = x + 6$, $y = 2x$, and $y = 3x$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x, y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions."}]}
